# Liquid Glass UI

Read `.cursor/skills/apple-inspired-ui/SKILL.md` and [true-glass-engine.md](../skills/apple-inspired-ui/references/true-glass-engine.md).

> **Blur isn't glass.** ([Outpace Studios](https://glass.outpacestudios.com/))  
> `backdrop-filter: blur()` = **frost chrome** (Tier A). Real liquid glass = **edge refraction** via SVG displacement (Tier B).

## Rule #1: Navigation Only

Glass (frost or lens) is **only** for: top bar, side panel chrome, tab bars, toolbars, menus, command palette, toasts, drawer scrim, secondary controls.

**Never** on: chat bubbles, timeline cards, graph nodes, tree rows, diff/code, harness cards, list items.

## Rule #2: Two Tiers

| Tier | CSS / component | Label in code |
|------|-----------------|---------------|
| **A — Frost chrome** | `backdrop-filter` + `--glass-bg-*` tokens | `frost-chrome` |
| **B — True lens** | `GlassScene` + `GlassLens` + `feDisplacementMap` | `glass-lens` |

```tsx
// ✅ Tier B — hero overlay (command palette, dropdown)
<GlassScene content={<AmbientBackdrop />}>
  {open && <GlassLens bounds={bounds}>{items}</GlassLens>}
</GlassScene>

// ✅ Tier A — bulk side panel (performance)
.panel {
  background: var(--glass-bg-clear);
  backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur-lg)) saturate(var(--glass-saturate));
}

// ❌ Tier B trap — SVG displacement via backdrop-filter (Safari/Firefox = flat frost only)
.menu { backdrop-filter: blur(20px) url(#glass-filter); }

// ✅ Content card — solid, no blur
.stepCard {
  background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  border: 1px solid var(--glass-border-subtle);
}
```

## Tier B Requirements (True Glass)

When implementing hero overlays:

1. **Refract a copy**, not live backdrop — `filter` on counter-positioned copy ([Outpace](https://glass.outpacestudios.com/))
2. Displacement map from **Snell's law** squircle dome — not painted gradient
3. `feImage` href = **`blob:` URL** — never `data:` (WebKit silent fail)
4. Filter `colorInterpolationFilters="sRGB"`
5. Clip copy to **lens box** (Safari size cap)
6. **Fresh filter `id`** per animated rebuild (Safari cache)
7. Chromium: optional chromatic fringe passes; Safari: single pass

Recipe: `.cursor/skills/apple-inspired-ui/components/glass-lens.md`

## Tier A Frost Tokens

| Style | Token | When |
|-------|-------|------|
| regular | `--glass-bg-regular` | Toolbars, side panels |
| clear | `--glass-bg-clear` | Over `--ambient-mesh` backgrounds |
| identity | solid `--color-bg-elevated` | `prefers-reduced-transparency` |

Place `--ambient-mesh` behind frost so blur has visible content to sample.

## GlassEffectContainer (Tier A)

Nearby frost elements share one parent blur. Max 2 blurred layers per viewport column.

## Interactive

- Primary: solid accent (glassProminent) — no blur, no lens
- Secondary: solid transparent inside glass container
- `:active` → `scale(0.98)`; `:focus-visible` → `--glass-focus-ring`
- Min hit target 44×32px on icon buttons

## Accessibility

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce) {
  .glass-nav, .glass-lens .refractCopy {
    backdrop-filter: none;
    filter: none;
  }
  .glass-nav, .glass-lens {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  }
}
```

Tier B: drop refraction entirely under reduced-transparency; UI stays on opaque panel.
